detailed_feedback: "The candidate shows promise in software engineering fundamentals and has some Python experience, particularly in algorithm development. Their work at JetBrains and Deutsche Börse demonstrates ability to work with complex systems and CI/CD pipelines.\n\nHowever, there are significant gaps in backend development expertise. The candidate lacks experience with FastAPI and related frameworks, has no demonstrated API design experience, and shows no evidence of working with databases. Their GitHub projects, while showing Python proficiency, focus more on algorithms than web development.\n\nThe candidate's experience level (2 years) is well below the senior requirement (5+ years), and they are still pursuing their Bachelor's degree. While they show potential, they would be better suited for a junior or mid-level position."
hiring_manager_notes: "This candidate does not meet the requirements for a Senior Backend Python Developer position. While they demonstrate good software engineering fundamentals and learning potential, they lack the necessary experience with backend technologies and frameworks specified in the job description.\n\nThe 2 years of experience and ongoing education suggest they are early in their career journey. Their background in IDE development (JetBrains) and infrastructure (Deutsche Börse) shows capability, but doesn't align closely with backend API development needs.\n\nRecommendation: Consider for junior/mid-level positions instead, or suggest reapplying after gaining more backend development experience with relevant technologies."